We compare TUON against representative optimizers from three levels of structural granularity. (i) AdamW ( Loshchilov & Hutter, 2017 ) is the de facto vector-aware standard for large-scale pretraining. (ii) Muon ( Jordan et al., 2024 ) is a matrix-aware optimizer that has recently demonstrated remarkable breakthroughs in LLM pretraining. (iii) TEON ( Zhang et al., 2026a ) is a recent tensor-aware optimizer that has consistently outperformed Muon across model scales and architectures. Tensorion is also a tensor-aware optimizer, but it has been validated mainly on vision tasks, so we use TEON rather than Tensorion as our tensor-aware baseline. Together, these baselines span vector-, matrix-, and tensor-level optimization. More details can be found in Appendix I.3 .

